.TH XD\-POWER 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-power \- Power Options Properties
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-power
.OP \-\-page n
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-power
is Windows XP's Power Options Properties (Control Panel):
.TP
.B Power Schemes
When to turn off the monitor, stand by and hibernate; with a battery
(through UPower), separately when plugged in and on batteries.
Schemes of the user's own are kept with Save As and Delete.
.TP
.B Alarms
With a battery, the low and critical battery alarms and their actions
(sound, message, stand by, hibernate or shut down).
.TP
.B Power Meter
With a battery, the power source and charge.
.TP
.B Advanced
The battery icon, locking the computer on resume, and what closing the
lid and pressing the power or sleep button do: this user's own choice,
logind's setting until one is made. Closing the lid does nothing while
another monitor is connected or the computer is docked.
.TP
.B Hibernate
Whether the computer can hibernate, and the space it needs.
.PP
.BR xd\-shell (1)
carries the settings out.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " n"
Open on the
.IR n th
tab shown, from 0 (Power Schemes).
Without a battery, Alarms and Power Meter aren't shown.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/desktop.ini
.B [Power]
and
.BR [ScreenSaver] .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-shell (1),
.BR xd\-control (1)
